L0218: Loop exit has the wrong shape

A while or for loop does not return a break payload in this core, and continue cannot carry a result. Store a result in an appropriate mutable binding or use a loop expression whose exit type explicitly permits a value.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/break_in_for.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// `break` with a value leaves a `while` or a `for`, which produce no value;
// only a `loop` has the value of its `break`.
fn first(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let mut total: u8 = 0;
    for i in 0..n {
        break total
    }
}

fn second(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let mut k: u8 = 0;
    while k < n {
        k = k.wrapping_add(1);
        break k
    }
    k
}
```

Language, as built: [1.12:3](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.12:3).
